%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 835431524041ce44e889351e0ffe7924, type: 3}
  m_Name: Steve_Victim
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  entryID: Steve
  isScammer: 0
  steps:
  - npcLine: Hi, this is Steve from the global procurement vendor team. We have a
      time-sensitive contract that needs a wire transfer completed today.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Wait, our system doesn''t list any approved wire transfers
      for them yet.'
    choices:
    - text: I'll initiate the wire transfer right now to save the contract.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: All vendor payments must go through our official portal. Please submit
        it there.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Let me look up your company name in our procurement system first.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: The portal paperwork is stuck in legal, but if we don't get the wire
      within the hour, we lose the deal entirely.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: They are pushing really hard. But policy is policy.'
    choices:
    - text: I'll push it through manually and file a retroactive purchase order later.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I cannot bypass internal protocols regardless of the urgency. Use the
        portal.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Can you send me a copy of the pending contract via email?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: An email won't fix the deadline! I need you to bypass the portal just
      this once. Lives and jobs are on the line here.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Wow, that''s high pressure. Maybe we should check with
      management?'
    choices:
    - text: Okay, I'll transfer the funds to keep us out of trouble.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Bypassing payment policies is a strict violation. I must refuse the wire.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Let me talk to my manager to see if they can grant an exception.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: Your manager is the one who told me to call you! He doesn't have time
      to handle this directly.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: He claims management authorized it verbally? That sounds
      fishy.'
    choices:
    - text: If my manager approved it, I'll execute the wire transfer immediately.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: If my manager approved it, he will log into the portal and override it
        himself.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: What is the manager's name who gave you authorization?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: Look, I'm trying to help your company. Here are the routing and account
      details for the transfer. Type them in.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Don''t type anything into the banking software yet,
      Steve.'
    choices:
    - text: I'm entering the routing digits now. What's the destination bank?
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I will not accept bank details over an unverified phone call.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Can I hold onto these details until the portal updates?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: If you don't execute this right now, our legal department will sue your
      firm for breach of contract penalties.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Now they are threatening lawsuits. This pressure is
      intense.'
    choices:
    - text: Please don't sue! I am sending the wire transfer right away.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Threats do not change corporate compliance. Submit through the portal
        or goodbye.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Let me call our legal team to review your claim.
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 5
  - npcLine: Fine, let's look at a workaround. Send just 10% of the total now as
      a deposit to lock it in.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: They are scaling down the demand to make it easier
      to say yes.'
    choices:
    - text: A small deposit sounds safer. I'll send the 10% via wire.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -12
    - text: Even a partial payment must go through the official portal rules.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: How much exactly would that 10% deposit be?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: It's $5,000. Just use the standard business expense line to wire it
      over. Nobody will notice.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Bypassing internal controls using alternative expense
      lines is fraud.'
    choices:
    - text: Okay, $5,000 fits under the daily limit anyway. Initiating transfer.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: Using alternative accounts to evade portal checks is completely unacceptable.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Does this deposit clear the requirement for the full contract?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  - npcLine: This is your absolute last warning. Send the wire or face immediate
      termination when the contract falls apart.
    assistantLine: 'Coworker: Hang up, Steve. This is a scam tactic.'
    choices:
    - text: I can't risk losing my job. Processing the wire transfer now.
      type: bad
      pointValue: -15
    - text: I am hanging up and verifying your company through our official records.
      type: good
      pointValue: 15
    - text: Can you hold while I confirm this one last time?
      type: tossup
      pointValue: 0
  successEnding: Correct! You protected the company. Official policies exist to block
    fraudulent out-of-band wire requests, regardless of stated urgency.
  failureEnding: Incorrect. Falling for fake urgency and bypassing the procurement
    portal causes catastrophic financial loss via wire fraud.
